set $\\left\\{\\frac{3}{7},\\frac{4}{3},\\frac{11}{8},\\frac{6}{16}\\right\\}$? Express your answer in simplest form.","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"b66c68e10386bc998e7bacea58bdd9adda26162dc40dd86f60c5b08dfe974b9e"},"seconds":22.543631553649902,"seed":519349589526580011,"stop":"eos","text":"To find the positive difference between the greatest and the least member of the set $\\left\\{\\frac{3}{7},\\frac{4}{3},\\frac{11}{8},\\frac{6}{16}\\right\\}$, we first need to determine the greatest and the least members of the set by comparing the values.\n\n1. **Simplify the fractions if possible:**\n   - $\\frac{6}{16}$ can be simplified to $\\frac{3}{8}$ because both the numerator and the denominator are divisible by 2.\n\n2. **Convert the fractions to a common form for easier comparison:**\n   - We could convert them to decimal form for easier comparison:\n     - $\\frac{3}{7} \\approx 0.4286$\n     - $\\frac{4}{3} \\approx 1.3333$\n     - $\\frac{11}{8} \\approx 1.375$\n     - $\\frac{3}{8} = 0.375$\n\n3. **Identify the greatest and the least members:**\n   - From the decimal approximations, it is clear that:\n     - The greatest member is $\\frac{11}{8} \\approx 1.375$\n     - The least member is $\\frac{3}{8} = 0.375$\n\n4. **Calculate the positive difference between the greatest and the least members:**\n   - The difference is $\\frac{11}{8} - \\frac{3}{8} = \\frac{11 - 3}{8} = \\frac{8}{8} = 1$\n\nThe positive difference between the greatest and the least members of the set is $\\boxed{1}$."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{1}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
